1
00:00:02,377 --> 00:00:04,587
(Howard:)Okay, Raj...

2
00:00:04,754 --> 00:00:07,214
(Howard:)...hand me the number six
Torx screwdriver.

3
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:10,093
(Sheldon:)Stop.

4
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,884
(Sheldon:)We can't do this. It's not right.

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,684
Sheldon, you have got two choices.

6
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:18,438
(Raj:)Put a bigger hard drive in the TiVo
or delete stuff before we go out of town.

7
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:21,481
(Sheldon:)But once you open the box,
you've voided the warranty.

8
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:26,108
(Sheldon:)The warranty is a sacred covenant
we've entered into with the manufacturer.

9
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:27,946
(Sheldon:)He offers to stand by his equipment.

10
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:31,651
(Sheldon:)We in return agree not to violate
the integrity of the internal hardware.

11
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:36,783
(Sheldon:)This little orange sticker is all that stands
between us and anarchy.

12
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,951
(Howard:)Okay,
then we won't touch the hard drive.

13
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:42,873
(Leonard:)We'll just erase the first season
of Battlestar.

14
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,633
(Sheldon(ripping off sticker):)There. We're outlaws.

15
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:52,056
- Here you go, Leonard. Is this big enough?
- It's perfect.

16
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:58,517
(Howard:)For taking daffodils to your unicorn.

17
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:01,102
(Leonard:)It's just for my notebooks.
Thanks, Penny.

